## 25. Database Security Standards
- Use device-local encrypted SQLite.
- Do not store plaintext sensitive values unnecessarily.
- Do not expose encryption keys through APIs.
- Do not log plaintext sensitive information or place real secrets into application logs.
- Do not send sensitive values unnecessarily to external services.
- Authorization must be enforced before real-value release.

